## Why This Is Asked

Assesses ability to design a robust, real-time data layer that stays responsive under network variability, using concurrency primitives and local caching.

## Key Concepts

- Swift concurrency with async/await and TaskGroups
- Local cache using SQLite
- Delta-based merge with per-item versioning
- Conflict resolution and ordering guarantees
- Test strategy for latency, reordering, and memory pressure

## Code Example

```swift
struct Post { let id: String; var version: Int; var content: String }
struct Delta { let id: String; let version: Int; let content: String }

func merge(_ deltas: [Delta], into cache: inout [String: Post]) -> [Post] {
  for d in deltas {
    if var existing = cache[d.id] {
      if d.version > existing.version {
        existing.version = d.version
        existing.content = d.content
        cache[d.id] = existing
      }
    } else {
      cache[d.id] = Post(id: d.id, version: d.version, content: d.content)
    }
  }
  return Array(cache.values)
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you detect and mitigate race conditions in the delta merge?
- How would you extend to multi-device sync and server-driven conflict resolution?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests familiarity with SwiftUI basics, timer handling, accessibility, and simple persistence in a beginner-friendly scenario.

## Key Concepts
- SwiftUI TimerPublisher and state management
- MVVM pattern with @ObservableObject and @Published
- UserDefaults for minimal persistence
- Accessibility: VoiceOver labels, Dynamic Type, color contrast
- Debouncing user input to prevent thrashing

## Code Example
```swift
class FocusTimerViewModel: ObservableObject {
  @Published var remaining: Int = 0
  @Published var isRunning: Bool = false
  private var cancellable: AnyCancellable?
  func start(duration: Int) {
    remaining = duration * 60
    isRunning = true
    cancellable = Timer.publish(every: 1, on: .main, in: .common)
      .autoconnect()
      .sink { [weak self] _ in
        guard let self = self else { return }
        if self.remaining > 0 { self.remaining -= 1 } else { self.isRunning = false }
      }
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle timer accuracy when the app is backgrounded?
- How would you scale to more than 3 presets and persist per-preset state?

